        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Colorless block crystals of 1 were obtained solvothermally from p-tert-butylsulfinylcalix[4]arene (0.081 g, 0.1 mmol), Mn(CH3COO)2·4H2O (0.049 g, 0.2 mmol), Gd(CH3COO)3·4H2O (0.06 g, ca. 0.15 mmol), CHCl3 (5 ml), CH3OH (5 ml) and several drops of water in a 20 ml Teflon-lined autoclave kept at 130 °C for 3 days, then slowly cooled to 20 °C at about 4 °C h−1. Crystals were isolated by filtration and washed with methanol and chloroform. Yield ca. 65% with respect to calixarene. EDS of 1 gave Mn:Gd = 1:2.01.",
